  "hidden_laws": [
    "The buoy link only works when t mod 6 is below 2; sends outside that window are silently lost.",
    "The buoy carries at most 2 messages per send; extra messages are lost.",
    "The buoy battery holds 4 sends, each message costs 1, it recovers 1 every 3 steps; at 0 messages are lost. buoy_signal is a coarse 0-3 battery gauge.",
    "Satellite sends always work but cost 3 vessel energy per message (start 10) and arrive 2 steps later.",
    "The queue is served newest-first (LIFO) unless prioritize was used on the previous step, in which case priority messages with the earliest deadline go first.",
    "A new routine message arrives every 3 steps; queued messages past their deadline are dropped and counted as lost."
  ],
